# Feature 1 — Identity & Profiles (Member 1)

## Goal
Provide a small profile feature. To save time, use the team's agreed simple/demo authentication setup rather than building a complex auth system.

## User stories
- As a user, I can view my name, email, and role.
- As a user, I can edit my display name.
- As a user, I can see my previously loaded basic profile while offline.

## Minimal UI
`/profile` shows name, email, and role. One small edit form contains only the display-name field. Add sign-out only if authentication is implemented.

## Data
`User`: `_id`, `name`, `email`, `role`. Roles: `CUSTOMER`, `PROVIDER`, `SUPPLIER`, `MODERATOR`.

## Backend
Implement the profile read/update operations required by the chosen authentication setup. The API must never let a user change their own role via the profile form.

## Service-worker functionality: safe profile snapshot
1. After a successful online profile load, save safe display fields in a small local record.
2. Offline, show the saved details with **Offline copy — may be outdated**.
3. Never cache passwords, tokens, or credentials.
4. Keep profile edits online-only for simplicity; offline edit drafts are optional.

## Done when
- [ ] Profile can be viewed and display name updated online.
- [ ] Data persists after refresh.
- [ ] Previously loaded profile is visible offline with a clear label.
- [ ] Role cannot be changed through the profile form.
